      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T19:31:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "btw I did some refactoring of rotate using 8 bit as a basis, making 16 and 32 bit elements work the same way.  Instead of \u0027scaling\u0027 to read a column and write a row, a tile is transposed.  The transpose is intended to scale with sve or sme, or rvv.  avx512/avx/sse are different tile sizes and in practice a common theme emerged - 4 int32 wide by vector length tall as a read, then 4 rows written.\nI\u0027m considering 24 bit, but that may be done a tile wrapper, allowing ld3 to be avoided.  on sve, rvv and avx512 masking helps avoid C.",
      "revId": "dc630852d7e90c27003ce0c7e322f7d02baff122",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
